// jsChar built from []rune(strAt(s,i))[0], so a LONE SURROGATE - half of an
// astral pair - becomes U+FFFD, which is exactly how the emitter's sw_gcount
// recognises a pair. That mapping is reproduced here rather than left to the
// engine, which would hand back the surrogate itself.
//
//  - The failure TEXT follows the Go twin (`string index %d out of range for %q`),
//    not swiftc: no Swift program can reach this fail. Swift's own subscript is
//    js_swidx; js_kindex is reached only from the emitter's own sw_gcount / sw_nfd
//    walks, whose loop bound is the same code-unit length the index counts in, and
//    from the variadic-parameter prologue, where the receiver is the args ARRAY.
//    swQuote stands in for Go's %q; the two differ only in how they escape a
//    control character.
//  - The returned TYPE differs from the twin: a one-character String, not a jsChar
