// can answer it - a conforming type's descriptor is named for itself, never for the
// protocol - so every adoption site writes a __conf_<P> marker on the very table a
// value reaches through __class, inherited protocols included, and this is the same
// __class/__super walk swFindMember does (which is what makes a SUBCLASS of a
// conforming class conform too).
//
// The third argument is the statically known list of BUILTIN type names an
// `extension Int: P` conformed. A builtin value has no descriptor to hold a marker
// and the emitter knows the list at emit time, so it is passed in rather than kept
// in a runtime registry. Twins: swConforms in languages/swift-interpreter.abnf,
// js_swconf in abnf/jsrtswift.go.
function js_swconf(v, pname, bnames) {
