// emitter decides by NAME which call sites can mean one, but that cannot be final:
// with `extension Int { func pid() }` beside a `struct S { func pid() }`,
// `S().pid()` must answer S's. So the receiver decides here, at run time, by exactly the interpreter's
// rule: a value that HAS a builtin member table takes the $ext$ table, and
// everything else takes the ordinary member call. Twin: js_swextcall in
// abnf/jsrtswift.go.
